+/// Complete an interrupted write of `bytes` into an existing regular file
+/// whose first `existing` bytes the caller has already judged equal to
+/// `bytes[..existing]` (J-RW r4 item 3.2, C-SUFFIX; unit J4a). Only the
+/// missing suffix `bytes[existing..]` is written, at offset `existing`: no
+/// existing byte is rewritten and nothing is truncated. Then the same
+/// verification as `write_new_regular_accounted`: the length by `fstat`,
+/// every byte read back from offset zero and compared, the end confirmed,
